1
00:00:00,156 --> 00:00:01,421
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,423 --> 00:00:02,990
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:04,313 --> 00:00:06,709
(Episode 36)

4
00:00:07,678 --> 00:00:09,678
(The Late Cha O Reum)

5
00:01:06,715 --> 00:01:10,816
O Reum, you were so precious,
even though I only knew you so briefly.

6
00:01:11,657 --> 00:01:12,883
I love you.

7
00:01:13,609 --> 00:01:15,362
Don't be in pain anymore.

8
00:01:20,195 --> 00:01:21,530
From your aunt.

9
00:01:41,221 --> 00:01:43,221
(The Late Cha O Reum)

10
00:02:12,414 --> 00:02:14,817
What? It opens just fine.

11
00:02:15,101 --> 00:02:17,484
I know. Why wouldn't it open for me?

12
00:02:18,495 --> 00:02:19,859
What are you doing?

13
00:02:20,182 --> 00:02:21,637
Making porridge.

14
00:02:22,022 --> 00:02:25,437
You need to eat something.
The others from the columbarium need food.

15
00:02:27,935 --> 00:02:30,203
I can't believe you're cooking
in my kitchen.

16
00:02:30,928 --> 00:02:32,716
Life really is unpredictable.

17
00:02:32,749 --> 00:02:34,806
Tell me about it.

18
00:02:35,288 --> 00:02:37,300
No need to say anything childish.

19
00:02:37,325 --> 00:02:39,186
Life really is unpredictable.

20
00:02:40,491 --> 00:02:41,927
Are you feeling any better?

21
00:02:42,634 --> 00:02:44,138
I made some plain porridge.

22
00:02:44,162 --> 00:02:46,962
I didn't add anything in case
it didn't suit a pregnant woman's tastes.

23
00:02:47,887 --> 00:02:48,998
Good thinking.

24
00:02:49,022 --> 00:02:51,597
Have at least three spoonfuls too.

25
00:02:52,676 --> 00:02:53,676
Thanks.

26
00:02:54,768 --> 00:02:56,505
You saved my life too.

27
00:02:56,950 --> 00:02:58,027
And...

28
00:02:59,547 --> 00:03:00,553
We...

29
00:03:01,111 --> 00:03:03,469
You won't kick us both out, will you?

30
00:03:04,289 --> 00:03:07,289
Is that why you're making porridge?

31
00:03:07,499 --> 00:03:09,503
- Because you're afraid I'll kick you out?
- Yeong Ju...

32
00:03:09,528 --> 00:03:11,667
Don't!

33
00:03:12,641 --> 00:03:13,752
You really...

34
00:03:14,162 --> 00:03:16,540
Even at a time like this,
you only think about yourself?

35
00:03:17,022 --> 00:03:20,618
They say people never change,
and you're really making me sick.

36
00:03:20,642 --> 00:03:23,065
What else can I do?
I'm just being realistic.

37
00:03:23,090 --> 00:03:24,442
Do you think I don't know your temper?

38
00:03:24,467 --> 00:03:26,886
Fine. As long as you know my temper.

39
00:03:27,053 --> 00:03:28,664
Get out! I can't stand the sight of you.

40
00:03:29,634 --> 00:03:31,306
If we'd only gotten the marrow sooner...

41
00:03:31,883 --> 00:03:34,319
If he'd gotten the transplant
when he still had more strength...

42
00:03:34,578 --> 00:03:36,922
Of course I can't help thinking
about that!

43
00:03:37,408 --> 00:03:39,676
Everyone came to you begging and pleading.

44
00:03:39,701 --> 00:03:40,941
Didn't you make a whole show of it?

45
00:03:40,966 --> 00:03:44,056
That was
after Ji Ni's marrow test, though.

46
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:46,668
You said Ji Ni had changed you,

47
00:03:46,693 --> 00:03:48,891
- that you'd reflected on everything.
- I was wrong about everything.

48
00:03:49,184 --> 00:03:51,304
Can't you see? It was all for nothing!

49
00:03:58,568 --> 00:03:59,776
Seriously...

50
00:04:22,995 --> 00:04:26,216
That's right. People don't really change.

51
00:04:26,855 --> 00:04:28,498
And I thought I could live with her.

52
00:04:29,449 --> 00:04:31,592
No Yeong Ju, you really screwed up again.

53
00:04:48,708 --> 00:04:49,737
Still not done?

54
00:04:50,829 --> 00:04:51,829
No.

55
00:04:52,247 --> 00:04:53,797
Looks like there's a lot of paperwork.

56
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:57,656
Thanks for coming all this way.

57
00:04:58,829 --> 00:04:59,957
It's nothing.

58
00:05:00,681 --> 00:05:03,792
I'm more grateful that you let me come.

59
00:05:05,689 --> 00:05:07,545
But I'm worried about Mai.

60
00:05:07,921 --> 00:05:09,987
She's so pale, and she's pregnant.

61
00:05:12,142 --> 00:05:14,014
I can't even think about the baby.

62
00:05:14,415 --> 00:05:16,834
I don't know how she'd take it.

63
00:05:53,505 --> 00:05:55,990
(Na Se Ri, your balance is 1,223 dollars.)

64
00:06:09,842 --> 00:06:11,739
Yes. Hello.

65
00:06:12,161 --> 00:06:15,014
I'm the person Park Ji Yeong
referred to before.

66
00:06:15,038 --> 00:06:16,722
I heard you're hiring part-time staff.

67
00:06:17,242 --> 00:06:19,512
Yes, I'm 174 centimeters tall.

68
00:06:20,158 --> 00:06:21,858
Yes. I understand.

69
00:06:21,883 --> 00:06:24,984
It comes with full benefits too, right?

70
00:06:26,592 --> 00:06:28,438
Okay.

71
00:06:37,446 --> 00:06:38,483
Yeong Ju!

72
00:06:38,958 --> 00:06:40,875
What are you doing?

73
00:06:41,822 --> 00:06:44,523
Throw all this out
before the kids get here.

74
00:06:45,230 --> 00:06:47,525
What if Mai comes looking for it?
Why are you touching it?

75
00:06:47,550 --> 00:06:50,163
Besides, O Reum's younger sibling
might be able to use it.

76
00:06:50,374 --> 00:06:51,885
You ignorant fool.

77
00:06:52,461 --> 00:06:54,880
All you know how to do is steal
someone else's husband.

78
00:06:54,904 --> 00:06:55,914
Yeong Ju, seriously!

79
00:06:55,939 --> 00:06:58,117
Do you think I have time
to worry about your feelings?

80
00:06:58,935 --> 00:07:01,552
Anyway, we're not passing these down.
Throw them out.

81
00:07:03,121 --> 00:07:04,775
How scary.

82
00:07:06,561 --> 00:07:08,109
Let me see.

83
00:07:11,721 --> 00:07:13,833
We really need to get out of here now.

84
00:07:25,736 --> 00:07:27,382
- You're back?
- What is this...

85
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:29,671
What are you doing?

86
00:07:31,322 --> 00:07:33,919
Why are you throwing away
our dear O Reum's things?

87
00:07:34,334 --> 00:07:36,457
This isn't O Reum.

88
00:07:36,488 --> 00:07:40,742
- And I'm not the one throwing them out...
- Shut up!

89
00:07:44,121 --> 00:07:45,191
Mom, are you okay?

90
00:07:46,049 --> 00:07:48,025
Why are you throwing these away?

91
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:50,524
It's not my idea.
Yeong Ju told me to throw them out!

92
00:07:51,808 --> 00:07:54,816
Why would I touch them?

93
00:07:56,052 --> 00:07:57,176
Let's go.

94
00:08:03,375 --> 00:08:07,773
O Reum, your mom's here.

95
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:10,504
Your mom's here. Don't worry.

96
00:08:11,842 --> 00:08:14,379
Mai, mom told her to throw them out.

97
00:08:14,381 --> 00:08:16,112
Why would she throw them out?

98
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:19,100
Why would she throw away
our dear O Reum's things?

99
00:08:24,575 --> 00:08:26,824
Don't touch O Reum's things.

100
00:08:29,495 --> 00:08:30,563
Okay.

101
00:08:38,750 --> 00:08:39,779
Are you okay?

102
00:08:39,804 --> 00:08:41,032
My back...

103
00:08:45,808 --> 00:08:47,775
I got hurt because of you.

104
00:08:52,386 --> 00:08:55,090
Mai saw her throwing away the toys.

105
00:09:05,569 --> 00:09:06,960
They were supposed to be thrown away.

106
00:09:07,176 --> 00:09:09,139
Why?

107
00:09:09,164 --> 00:09:12,267
What do you know? You don't know anything!

108
00:09:13,089 --> 00:09:15,240
Whenever I leave a knife out,
you always take it away.

109
00:09:15,888 --> 00:09:19,615
Everything that's happened to O Reum
is because of you!

110
00:09:20,042 --> 00:09:21,326
Mai.

111
00:09:21,579 --> 00:09:23,318
Don't act like you're so perfect.

112
00:09:24,095 --> 00:09:25,659
What's the point of acting so refined...

113
00:09:25,947 --> 00:09:27,966
when you're secretly dating someone?

114
00:09:30,527 --> 00:09:32,482
You ignore everything I say.

115
00:09:33,316 --> 00:09:34,946
- You're so stubborn.
- Mai.

116
00:09:35,130 --> 00:09:36,220
What's gotten into you?

117
00:09:36,897 --> 00:09:38,552
You shut up too!

118
00:09:38,577 --> 00:09:40,663
When have you ever taken my side?

119
00:09:41,024 --> 00:09:43,528
Even when I ask you to move out,
it's always "Mom, Mom!"

120
00:09:45,488 --> 00:09:46,938
You're such a mama's boy.

121
00:09:58,221 --> 00:09:59,285
Mom.

122
00:09:59,665 --> 00:10:03,063
If I were actually dating someone,
I wouldn't feel so wronged.

123
00:10:30,309 --> 00:10:33,457
O Reum, I miss you.

124
00:10:44,295 --> 00:10:45,368
I have time.

125
00:10:45,761 --> 00:10:47,945
I'll head out. Yes.

126
00:10:50,981 --> 00:10:51,981
Seung Hyun.

127
00:10:52,678 --> 00:10:53,874
Mai's asleep.

128
00:10:54,602 --> 00:10:56,279
I'm afraid she'll wake up
if I stay beside her.

129
00:10:57,376 --> 00:10:58,660
You said you were heading out.

130
00:10:59,349 --> 00:11:00,349
Yeah.

131
00:11:08,642 --> 00:11:09,717
Are you okay?

132
00:11:12,508 --> 00:11:15,167
I take things in stride. You know that.

133
00:11:33,001 --> 00:11:34,001
England?

134
00:11:34,344 --> 00:11:37,127
Yes, my mom says she'll book the flight.

135
00:11:37,755 --> 00:11:38,992
First class.

136
00:11:39,838 --> 00:11:41,800
First class? Isn't that a bit much?

137
00:11:41,809 --> 00:11:45,208
Your future mother-in-law knows
how to treat her daughter's boyfriend.

138
00:11:45,782 --> 00:11:48,425
But I don't know exactly
when my summer vacation will be.

139
00:11:48,450 --> 00:11:50,343
You're worrying for nothing.

140
00:11:50,561 --> 00:11:53,748
Whatever dates you choose will work.
You know my dad.

141
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:57,082
My dad wants us to go yachting
and play some golf this time.

142
00:11:57,475 --> 00:12:00,487
I told him not to worry
because you're good at handling yachts.

143
00:12:01,050 --> 00:12:02,301
I'm so excited.

144
00:12:05,202 --> 00:12:07,226
You're the only one excited, aren't you?

145
00:12:07,575 --> 00:12:09,269
Could you mind your own business?

146
00:12:09,294 --> 00:12:12,437
You're so loud, everyone can hear you.

147
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:15,090
Ask the other customers...

148
00:12:15,115 --> 00:12:17,682
if there's anyone who doesn't know
you're going to England.

149
00:12:22,895 --> 00:12:25,755
Ji Hu, was I really that loud?

150
00:12:26,922 --> 00:12:29,145
I guess I got a little too excited.

151
00:12:34,128 --> 00:12:35,356
Going to England?

152
00:12:37,008 --> 00:12:38,426
Okay, I got it.

153
00:12:38,781 --> 00:12:39,819
Is that why you called?

154
00:12:39,844 --> 00:12:42,449
Are you kidding?
Why would I call about that?

155
00:12:43,968 --> 00:12:45,523
How's Ji Ni doing?

156
00:12:45,869 --> 00:12:48,782
She came to work after the funeral,
so please make sure she eats.

157
00:12:48,807 --> 00:12:50,598
I'm already looking out for her.

158
00:12:50,851 --> 00:12:52,783
Okay. Bye.

159
00:13:04,655 --> 00:13:05,671
Are you tired?

160
00:13:07,945 --> 00:13:09,772
Yes, a little.

161
00:13:09,797 --> 00:13:11,553
How about lunch before we continue?

162
00:13:12,422 --> 00:13:13,805
I don't have much of an appetite.

163
00:13:13,830 --> 00:13:16,293
Jung A told me to make sure you eat.

164
00:13:16,406 --> 00:13:18,560
Let's go.
I'll treat you to something good.

165
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:21,500
Okay.

166
00:13:22,475 --> 00:13:24,288
- I'll wash my hands first.
- Sure.

167
00:13:38,303 --> 00:13:40,303
(Stem Cell Donation Certificate)

168
00:13:47,835 --> 00:13:48,835
Tae O.

169
00:13:50,031 --> 00:13:51,343
Hey, you're here.

170
00:13:52,211 --> 00:13:54,343
- I heard you're going to London.
- How...

171
00:13:55,202 --> 00:13:56,662
Jung A must've told you.

172
00:13:57,628 --> 00:13:59,098
Looks like I'll be going.

173
00:13:59,682 --> 00:14:01,254
Do you love Do Hee?

174
00:14:02,222 --> 00:14:03,289
Why ask that all of a sudden?

175
00:14:04,294 --> 00:14:05,370
Tell me.

176
00:14:05,688 --> 00:14:07,882
What does Do Hee mean to you?

177
00:14:08,905 --> 00:14:12,126
You know what I was going through
when I left for London.

178
00:14:12,469 --> 00:14:15,294
After giving up the piano,
I was barely hanging on.

179
00:14:15,504 --> 00:14:17,018
Do Hee made me smile again.

180
00:14:17,184 --> 00:14:19,918
Shouldn't I be willing to endure this
for her?

181
00:14:20,629 --> 00:14:23,192
Love isn't a test of endurance.

182
00:14:23,441 --> 00:14:26,051
What's wrong with you?
Why are you suddenly acting like this?

183
00:14:29,393 --> 00:14:30,393
Here.

184
00:14:34,204 --> 00:14:35,604
(Stem Cell Donation Certificate, Na Ji Ni)

185
00:14:35,755 --> 00:14:36,768
Na Ji Ni?

186
00:14:37,889 --> 00:14:38,889
What's this?

187
00:14:39,622 --> 00:14:41,608
I found it in the trash
at Do Hee's art studio.

188
00:14:41,882 --> 00:14:43,664
It was inside Ji Ni's tablet case.

189
00:14:44,168 --> 00:14:46,588
So Do Hee really did steal it.

190
00:14:46,862 --> 00:14:48,101
I still can't believe it.

191
00:14:49,675 --> 00:14:50,675
Does Ji Ni know?

192
00:14:51,195 --> 00:14:52,581
I haven't told her yet.

193
00:14:52,908 --> 00:14:54,697
She came in after O Reum's funeral today.

194
00:14:54,771 --> 00:14:58,201
She spent all day crying and working
and barely managed to leave.

195
00:14:58,375 --> 00:15:00,401
How could I tell her?
Do you want her to collapse again?

196
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:03,008
Did you really find it at Do Hee's place?

197
00:15:04,408 --> 00:15:07,201
Believe me, I wish I hadn't seen it.

198
00:15:07,715 --> 00:15:10,288
Why would Do Hee do something like this?

199
00:15:10,788 --> 00:15:12,888
She may be competitive,
but she's crossed the line.

200
00:15:16,075 --> 00:15:17,879
My head's been a mess all day,

201
00:15:18,307 --> 00:15:19,910
and now you're going to England.

202
00:15:20,224 --> 00:15:21,370
Fine. That's enough.

203
00:15:22,928 --> 00:15:24,494
Hey, what are you doing?

204
00:15:25,614 --> 00:15:26,874
I just managed to flatten it out.

205
00:15:30,301 --> 00:15:31,441
Ji Ni...

206
00:15:32,762 --> 00:15:34,861
said this meant more to her
than her tablet.

207
00:15:35,868 --> 00:15:37,328
But it was in Do Hee's trash...

208
00:15:37,455 --> 00:15:39,375
torn up and crumpled...

209
00:15:47,295 --> 00:15:48,395
Ji Hu...

210
00:16:06,902 --> 00:16:08,614
Why are you so eager to work?

211
00:16:09,182 --> 00:16:10,381
I'm going out of my mind.

212
00:16:11,028 --> 00:16:12,948
I need to push myself just to keep going.

213
00:16:13,221 --> 00:16:15,469
I'll do anything.
Give me all the work you have.

214
00:16:15,471 --> 00:16:16,601
I'm happy to hear that.

215
00:16:18,848 --> 00:16:20,022
"Love in Zip."

216
00:16:20,173 --> 00:16:23,175
Isn't "Love in Zip" a little childish?

217
00:16:23,177 --> 00:16:25,608
Classy doesn't sell.
We're going for something childish.

218
00:16:25,895 --> 00:16:28,161
Besides, love is childish by nature.

219
00:16:28,482 --> 00:16:29,603
It can mean "Love in Zip,"

220
00:16:29,778 --> 00:16:30,789
or "Is it love?" in Korean.

221
00:16:30,950 --> 00:16:32,101
That's the wordplay.

222
00:16:33,342 --> 00:16:35,029
Were you always like this?

223
00:16:35,495 --> 00:16:36,786
Why are you being so cheesy?

224
00:16:36,967 --> 00:16:38,341
Just read it, okay?

225
00:16:39,166 --> 00:16:40,661
I told you, I'm doing it no matter what.

226
00:16:40,956 --> 00:16:42,881
Give me the contract.
We're the directing team, right?

227
00:16:43,096 --> 00:16:44,348
Will you be directing it?

228
00:16:46,762 --> 00:16:48,793
Of course. You're the producer.

229
00:16:48,852 --> 00:16:50,865
I've never done this before. No way.

230
00:16:50,867 --> 00:16:52,288
I'll be the assistant director.

231
00:16:52,948 --> 00:16:55,095
We have plenty of assistant directors.

232
00:16:55,663 --> 00:16:56,801
You direct it.

233
00:16:57,022 --> 00:16:58,495
You know how women think.

234
00:17:00,609 --> 00:17:03,065
- Are you being sarcastic?
- Why would I be?

235
00:17:03,279 --> 00:17:04,614
I'm asking for your help.

236
00:17:05,148 --> 00:17:06,679
Besides, you said you'd do anything.

237
00:17:07,107 --> 00:17:10,361
Give it a shot.
Nobody starts out experienced.

238
00:17:11,422 --> 00:17:12,428
Seriously.

239
00:17:13,455 --> 00:17:16,394
How's the casting going?
You said three men and three women.

240
00:17:16,422 --> 00:17:17,495
It's more or less settled.

241
00:17:19,676 --> 00:17:20,909
This one's Do Do Hee.

242
00:17:21,047 --> 00:17:24,745
She doesn't have enough followers yet
to really be called an influencer,

243
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:26,931
but her photos suggest
she's from a wealthy family.

244
00:17:27,114 --> 00:17:28,205
She's pretty too.

245
00:17:31,368 --> 00:17:32,508
Do Do Hee.

246
00:17:35,535 --> 00:17:37,620
- She's covered in designer labels.
- Exactly.

247
00:17:37,828 --> 00:17:39,693
A Luxury Girl, an Art Girl,
and a Strong-Minded Girl.

248
00:17:39,695 --> 00:17:41,127
Those are the three types I want.

249
00:17:42,448 --> 00:17:44,548
- Sounds good.
- Right?

250
00:17:44,681 --> 00:17:46,968
It's good to have you on the team.

251
00:17:47,728 --> 00:17:51,280
And here are the male candidates so far.

252
00:17:54,115 --> 00:17:55,197
An influencer,

253
00:17:56,284 --> 00:17:57,284
a model,

254
00:17:57,986 --> 00:17:59,248
and a former idol.

255
00:17:59,381 --> 00:18:01,235
So they're all aspiring celebrities?

256
00:18:01,322 --> 00:18:04,106
People will call the show fake
if we cast people like that these days.

257
00:18:04,174 --> 00:18:05,174
You think so?

258
00:18:05,582 --> 00:18:07,788
Well, I'll look into it.

259
00:18:35,248 --> 00:18:36,792
Welcome.

260
00:18:40,347 --> 00:18:42,094
You look amazing.

261
00:18:42,108 --> 00:18:44,426
I bet you'd look good in anything.

262
00:18:44,428 --> 00:18:47,035
Our dresses are very popular.
Why don't you pick one?

263
00:18:47,788 --> 00:18:50,690
I called ahead.
I'm here for an appointment.

264
00:18:52,931 --> 00:18:54,409
Are you here for the part-time job?

265
00:18:59,269 --> 00:19:02,609
(Yeong Ju, is O Reum...)

266
00:19:03,448 --> 00:19:04,742
No.

267
00:19:07,585 --> 00:19:08,585
Again.

268
00:19:14,375 --> 00:19:15,375
Yes.

269
00:19:17,482 --> 00:19:19,640
Doctor, aren't you heading home?

270
00:19:20,074 --> 00:19:22,391
You go ahead. Good work today.

271
00:19:22,698 --> 00:19:23,698
Yes.

272
00:19:59,835 --> 00:20:01,149
(Im Sa Bin)

273
00:20:11,441 --> 00:20:16,428
The person you are calling is unavailable.
Please leave a message after the beep...

274
00:20:49,655 --> 00:20:50,709
Sa Bin.

275
00:20:51,690 --> 00:20:53,860
I came at the wrong time, right?

276
00:20:54,354 --> 00:20:55,948
I made you uncomfortable, right? I'll go.

277
00:20:55,950 --> 00:20:58,215
No, it's okay.

278
00:21:17,122 --> 00:21:18,301
O Reum...

279
00:21:19,448 --> 00:21:21,328
I saw him off.

280
00:21:24,095 --> 00:21:25,553
You didn't collapse, right?

281
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:27,195
I was worried.

282
00:21:28,135 --> 00:21:31,297
I was afraid you'd collapse and cry again.

283
00:21:31,737 --> 00:21:32,949
I'm okay.

284
00:21:33,961 --> 00:21:35,341
You don't have to worry.

285
00:21:37,348 --> 00:21:39,691
I'm sorry I didn't answer your call.

286
00:21:42,782 --> 00:21:43,877
Lately,

287
00:21:44,675 --> 00:21:47,373
I've been listening to a song called
"I Want to Know."

288
00:21:47,942 --> 00:21:51,335
It asks if someone would be happy
to hear from you when they're busy.

289
00:21:51,892 --> 00:21:53,303
That's what it's about.

290
00:21:55,197 --> 00:21:56,511
Sa Bin.

291
00:22:00,408 --> 00:22:04,201
I want to be part of your family.

292
00:22:07,075 --> 00:22:08,508
Really, thank you.

293
00:22:09,837 --> 00:22:11,224
In a few days,

294
00:22:12,165 --> 00:22:13,941
I'll go back to the singing class.

295
00:22:16,375 --> 00:22:17,554
Please come.

296
00:22:18,631 --> 00:22:19,895
I'll be waiting.

297
00:22:29,115 --> 00:22:30,566
You're finally here.

298
00:22:33,302 --> 00:22:34,302
Yes.

299
00:22:41,495 --> 00:22:43,764
I'll get going.

300
00:22:51,986 --> 00:22:53,637
Don't lose heart.

301
00:23:45,088 --> 00:23:46,564
Thank you.

302
00:23:47,855 --> 00:23:49,968
It's been so long since I've been here.

303
00:23:51,449 --> 00:23:54,489
I haven't been drinking lately
because I felt awkward around Ji Ni.

304
00:23:56,947 --> 00:23:58,759
You don't carry your cello around anymore?

305
00:24:00,002 --> 00:24:01,719
I didn't just come from a lesson.

306
00:24:02,262 --> 00:24:03,486
I found another part-time job.

307
00:24:03,807 --> 00:24:06,955
- Another part-time job?
- I can't teach with my wrist shaking.

308
00:24:08,308 --> 00:24:09,814
What kind of job is it?

309
00:24:10,182 --> 00:24:11,182
It's a secret.

310
00:24:12,042 --> 00:24:13,795
Are you here to see Yeong Ju?

311
00:24:15,782 --> 00:24:17,280
We didn't even see each other
for five minutes.

312
00:24:18,444 --> 00:24:19,615
I see.

313
00:24:20,135 --> 00:24:22,828
Is she having a hard time at home?

314
00:24:24,288 --> 00:24:27,301
What could be so hard?
She's the lady of the house.

315
00:24:27,875 --> 00:24:29,893
After O Reum passed away,

316
00:24:29,934 --> 00:24:32,868
I felt awkward, so I thought
I should save up as fast as I could.

317
00:24:33,482 --> 00:24:37,451
Somehow, she seemed worried
about what her sons thought.

318
00:24:37,968 --> 00:24:39,619
Am I being too sensitive?

319
00:24:39,715 --> 00:24:42,921
So that's why you wanted to come here?
To see what the family was like.

320
00:24:43,502 --> 00:24:44,906
Do you think her sons...

321
00:24:45,101 --> 00:24:47,374
don't like her seeing me?

322
00:24:48,348 --> 00:24:51,765
Did you expect them to welcome you?

323
00:24:54,920 --> 00:24:58,068
I have a job. I'm not that old...

324
00:24:58,555 --> 00:25:00,475
You're just a young prince.

325
00:25:00,688 --> 00:25:02,457
You're really young, Sa Bin.

326
00:25:04,134 --> 00:25:05,294
Me?

327
00:25:06,148 --> 00:25:09,115
To her sons, their mom is just their mom.

328
00:25:09,662 --> 00:25:14,092
They don't think their mom needs
a younger man with a job.

329
00:25:14,295 --> 00:25:16,447
That only applies
if it's her first marriage.

330
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:25,292
This is your first time
being rejected, right?

331
00:25:26,313 --> 00:25:27,335
I guess so.

332
00:25:28,081 --> 00:25:30,401
It's not like I've ever had
a reason to be rejected before.

333
00:25:30,875 --> 00:25:32,089
I just figured...

334
00:25:32,430 --> 00:25:34,916
my brother would object,
so I'd have to convince him.

335
00:25:35,517 --> 00:25:38,375
- That's about all I expected.
- Fair enough.

336
00:25:39,875 --> 00:25:42,981
But is she really serious about you?

337
00:25:43,495 --> 00:25:46,788
That's how it feels to me,
but I'm not sure yet.

338
00:25:47,228 --> 00:25:48,741
Doesn't it seem that way to you?

339
00:25:50,861 --> 00:25:51,898
Sa Bin,

340
00:25:52,559 --> 00:25:54,701
don't take this the wrong way.

341
00:25:55,075 --> 00:26:00,412
You can't even force a newborn to eat.

342
00:26:00,481 --> 00:26:02,503
It'll push food away with its tiny tongue.

343
00:26:02,944 --> 00:26:04,975
- Right.
- Exactly.

344
00:26:05,248 --> 00:26:08,540
When people really want something,
they'll do it no matter what anyone says.

345
00:26:08,542 --> 00:26:09,957
Just like you.

346
00:26:10,615 --> 00:26:14,616
If Yeong Ju wants to focus on her family,

347
00:26:15,030 --> 00:26:16,502
that may be what she truly wants.

348
00:26:16,595 --> 00:26:18,341
You should respect that too.

349
00:26:18,382 --> 00:26:20,742
Am I overreacting? Am I being selfish?

350
00:26:21,542 --> 00:26:23,324
I can't say for sure,

351
00:26:23,472 --> 00:26:27,415
Even I'd worry about what Ji Ni thought,
let alone Yeong Ju.

352
00:26:28,008 --> 00:26:30,981
She probably wouldn't budge
if her sons were against it.

353
00:26:31,968 --> 00:26:34,308
That's just my opinion, though.

354
00:26:52,668 --> 00:26:53,985
Is Mai still asleep?

355
00:26:54,895 --> 00:26:55,984
She...

356
00:26:56,585 --> 00:26:58,380
woke up earlier too,

357
00:26:58,740 --> 00:27:00,687
crying and looking for O Reum.

358
00:27:03,182 --> 00:27:04,182
Mom.

359
00:27:04,539 --> 00:27:05,539
Yeah?

360
00:27:06,697 --> 00:27:07,697
For now,

361
00:27:08,428 --> 00:27:09,795
don't see him.

362
00:27:10,595 --> 00:27:11,968
I wasn't seeing him.

363
00:27:12,242 --> 00:27:13,942
I wasn't answering my phone, so...

364
00:27:16,575 --> 00:27:17,735
Why are you acting like this too?

365
00:27:17,738 --> 00:27:19,336
Honestly,

366
00:27:19,650 --> 00:27:21,035
I don't mind.

367
00:27:21,495 --> 00:27:23,642
But seeing you with him,

368
00:27:24,596 --> 00:27:26,467
I don't think now's the right time.

369
00:27:27,001 --> 00:27:29,684
Just imagine if Seung Hyun saw you.
You wouldn't hear the end of it.

370
00:27:29,686 --> 00:27:31,688
What did I even do?

371
00:27:35,061 --> 00:27:36,908
- Fine. I get it.
- I'm...

372
00:27:37,209 --> 00:27:38,855
not against you dating.

373
00:27:38,975 --> 00:27:39,993
But...

374
00:27:40,514 --> 00:27:42,984
wait a little. Take it slow.

375
00:27:43,298 --> 00:27:44,615
What's the rush?

376
00:27:46,383 --> 00:27:48,678
- O Reum just passed away...
- I said I get it.

377
00:27:49,112 --> 00:27:50,775
Stop lecturing me.

378
00:28:10,156 --> 00:28:13,474
(Family Register)

379
00:28:13,571 --> 00:28:14,846
Do you need love?

380
00:28:14,848 --> 00:28:16,086
Of course I do.

381
00:28:16,088 --> 00:28:17,622
Am I supposed to die
being nothing but a grandma?

382
00:28:17,624 --> 00:28:19,248
I think the owner seems pretty nice.

383
00:28:19,250 --> 00:28:21,362
Doesn't she fit what we're looking for?

384
00:28:21,364 --> 00:28:22,915
Nothing comes without a price.

385
00:28:22,917 --> 00:28:24,553
You don't get anything by sitting around.

386
00:28:24,555 --> 00:28:26,168
I don't know where to even start.

387
00:28:26,170 --> 00:28:28,488
If you keep dragging this out,
I'll tell Ji Ni.

388
00:28:28,491 --> 00:28:30,688
It needs to be more vibrant
than the original painting.

389
00:28:30,690 --> 00:28:32,502
Different enough to stand out at a glance.

390
00:28:34,494 --> 00:28:36,494
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
